    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining the current AMZN position without adding new capital. The technical picture is objectively bullish \u2014 golden cross intact, positive MACD, RSI at 63.35, and +22.69% over 60 days with a shallow -1.54% drawdown \u2014 supported by strong cash generation ($84.95B operating cash flow). However, the stock is extended 25.4% above the 200-day SMA near the upper Bollinger Band after a strong run, and the April 12 session showed a distribution pattern (lower close than open, $3.64 off the intraday high). The risk/reward is asymmetric to the downside (-5.5% to 50-day support vs +1.6% to upper Bollinger), and fundamental data (income statement, margins, valuation) is unavailable in this historical run, creating a data vacuum that argues against conviction either way. This balanced evidence \u2014 powerful uptrend on one side, extended entry with no fundamental confirmation on the other \u2014 is the definition of a Hold: maintain the position, don't chase, and wait for either a pullback to the $175.95-$180.97 accumulation zone or fundamental confirmation before committing more capital.\n\n**Entry Price**: 186.13\n\n**Stop Loss**: 179.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-moderate weight; do not overweight until a pullback to $175.95-$180.97 support or fundamental confirmation occurs.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
